I never had wished for a quest artifact before, but as I said, the
fever caught me. I remember reading some posts about how the PYEC is a
nice wish for neutrals, so I wished for it. It was good for the
telepathy (but I would as well had wished for [HoT) and the MR (but I
wished for GDSM too). I didn't #invoked it too much; recharged some
wands and it was all. I didn't want to wish for the "EoA because I
didn't want to transform the ranger into a spellslinger, if you see my
point; just being able to cast some spells, preferably the ones
rangers have skills (div.,escape,healing). I wanted to do it 'the
ranger way', so no mjollnir and the like. After getting some advice
and thinking a lot, I wasted the three first wishes in 2b?oCharging,
PYEC and GDSM (I should have wished for SDSM, since one source of MR
at that point was more than needed. sigh.)
For a good weapon I thought of Cleaver -- yes, it may not be a
1st-class artifact weapon, but fitted 'the ranger way' style; see the
post were I asked for advices. But in the end it was MB. Then I wished
for a [SoR for my reflection needs and saved the other wishes for
after.

So I finished sokoban (another BoH) and started to go down. I was with
a half AK in hands, so I decided to go genocideless, since I always
genocide h,L,R before going down. Faced a rust monster and my MB
become rusted (yes, I *forgot* to wish for rustproof MB). Dang!! Well
at least I had a good supply of throwing weapons and enough skills on
them. Shortly after I did a saccfest around lvl 11 IIRC and got Vorpal
Blade. Cool! Never had put my hands on it before. A shame I just could
get basic at it. Rusted MB was in my pocket and I went with Vorpy the
rest of the game. Finished the mines and got teleport control and
teleportitis from tengus (in that order :) . Reached Medusa, no means
of levitating or whatsoever so got back to try the quest. I was xplvl
13, but maybe I could find some [WWB. I did not, but collected a lot
of arrows from those centaurs. So I just wished for [WWB and get down
again. Killed Medusa, lowered the drawbridge the hard way (yes,
guessing notes, only for the fun :) killed some monsters, got the 2nd
/oW. I wanted to wish for [GoD and [HoB, but I hoped for finding them
in the castle armory. No way to jump or levitate the holes (slapped my
forehead). Oh my. I got down until finding Asmodeus level. Got back,
up in the dungeons to my early stashes, brought some stuff, did the
quest, got a lot of arrows and the Longbow of Diana, all the time
hoping for finding levitation (potion, ring, boots, whatever). Did
not. Went back to the castle. Wished for a MM (to enchant up armor and
weapons), a spellbook of identify, [GoD, [HoB, and I can't remember
what more. Later on at Gehennom I found [JB and was able to go to the
castle's storerooms (nothing useful there).

Found few spellbooks of what I wanted through the game - got healing,
stone to flesh, identify, force bolt, and some others. Some of these I
found more than one copy (bestsellers?). No magic mapping, jumping,
haste self, levitation, teleport away, and the like. In retrospect I
think I should had wished for a /oPoly to polypile my vast collection
of duplicated spellbooks to get the ones I wanted, since I found no
/oPoly in the entire game. At least I had my trusty teleportitis.

Down to Gehennom again. Got through Asmo, Juiblex, Baalzebub (this one
escaped upstairs and I let him to kill in the final run). Then I
reached Orcus town. I went through some vampires, then came one with a
/oCreateMonster, which he promptly used. Some monsters appeard, I
killed the vampire, blindly got the wand, and then I made my final
incredibly stupid move: since I had throwed away lots of wands (in
Gehennom it rains wands, isn't it?) I had the bright idea of breaking
_that_ last wand I just picked up to cause some damage in the
surrounding monsters. Ho hum. So I did. And the party begun! An
anonymous & was kind enough to summon Yeenoghu, so the party was
complete.
My stupidity alarm sounded, but it was too late. "The foo hits! The
foo hits!" a thousand times and my HP halved down. I was using =oReg
and =oFA (because of shades), but the regeneration was not enough.
Only one !oFH (IIRC) in my main inventory; totally surrounded, with no
means to retreat; and could not teleport as well. Quaffed the !oFH but
my HP was going down very fast; spent some turns taking off the =oFA
to put the conflict one, what gave me some more moments to breath,
while the monsters fight one another, but obviously some of them kept
attacking me. Including Yeenoghu.

Yeenoghu swings its flail.  Yeenoghu hits!  Yeenoghu swings its
